AB  - This study discusses the adoption of Robotic Process Automation (RPA) within Agile methods, focusing on its transformational impact on software development practices. Agile's nature of being iterative and flexible is well suited to the automation of repetitive, rule-based tasks by RPA to streamline workflows and increase efficiency. RPA removes bottlenecks and frees up teams from testing, data migration, and reporting mundane work to focus on high-value, strategic activities. This synergy helps in improving the delivery cycles, enhancing productivity, and high-quality software. The study researches strategies, challenges, and outcomes related to this integration, which emphasizes frameworks, such as Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD), which allows automation deployment in an iterative, reliable manner. Emerging technologies, such as Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Cloud Computing, further enhance RPA capabilities by offering scalability, cognitive insights, and adaptability to dynamic project requirements, which enables Agile teams to maintain velocity while responding promptly to changing customer demands. By reviewing metrics and Key Performance Indicators such as velocity, sprint completion rates, ROI, and customer satisfaction, this study will evaluate RPA's effectiveness in supporting Agile goals. Real-world applications will show how these two may come together to ensure organizational agility and resilience. Insights presented can help practitioners better employ RPA in Agile workflows for optimizing scalability and maintaining continuous improvement.
ER  - 

