AB  - This paper presents ML-DaaS, a novel Deployment-as-a-Service framework designed for Machine Learning model training and deployment across hybrid cloud environments. Addressing the complexity of traditional MLOps workflows, ML-DaaS allows authenticated users to securely upload, train, finetune, and deploy ML models via an intuitive browser-based dashboard. The framework incorporates DevOps Tools such as Terraform, Ansible, Docker, and Jenkins, which automates infrastructure provisioning, system configuration, and CI/CD deployment, dynamically transitioning models from GPU-based training environments to cost-effective CPU-based inference. Experimental evaluations on OpenStack-based private clouds and AWS public cloud demonstrate the framework's consistent performance, secure isolation, and low-latency inference capabilities, thereby significantly reducing deployment complexity and operational overhead. Decoupling training from inference resulted in optimized resource utilization without sacrificing responsiveness, resulting in up to 40 % improvement in infrastructure turnaround time and a significant reduction in deployment complexity and operational overhead.
